# Clozer × FundsVerifier integration — environment variables
#
# Add these to Funds-Verifier-2026-Back-End-Final/.env

```env
# Shared secret for Clozer server-to-server API calls
CLOZER_API_KEY=your_shared_api_key_for_clozer_server_calls

# HMAC secret for installment webhook signatures
CLOZER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_webhook_signing_secret

# HMAC secret for redirect URL tokens (also share with Clozer to verify locally)
CLOZER_REDIRECT_SECRET=your_redirect_token_signing_secret

# Clozer hosted application form URL
CLOZER_APPLY_URL=https://clozer.ae/apply

# Pay-in-full discount (percent). Clozer installments always use full invoice amount.
FULL_PAY_DISCOUNT_PERCENT=5
```

Optional frontend (defaults work if backend returns redirectUrl):

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_FULL_PAY_DISCOUNT_PERCENT=5
```

---

## Handoff checklist (give these to Clozer)

| # | Item | Value |
|---|------|-------|
| 1 | API base URL | `https://YOUR-API-HOST/api` (e.g. production or staging) |
| 2 | Authentication | `Authorization: Bearer {CLOZER_API_KEY}` **or** `X-API-Key: {CLOZER_API_KEY}` |
| 3 | API credentials | Share `CLOZER_API_KEY`, `CLOZER_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `CLOZER_REDIRECT_SECRET` securely |
| 4 | Transaction details | `GET /api/clozer/transactions/{transaction_id}` |
| 5 | Installment updates | `POST /api/clozer/installment-updates` |
| 6 | Redirect token verify (optional) | `GET /api/clozer/verify-redirect/{transaction_id}?token={token}` |
| 7 | Sample data (dev only) | `GET /api/clozer/sample-transaction` |
| 8 | Sandbox | Use your staging API URL; webhook signature optional when `NODE_ENV !== production` |

---

## Integration flow

1. Customer selects **Pay by Installments with Clozer** in FundsVerifier.
2. FundsVerifier backend creates a transaction and returns redirect URL:
   `https://clozer.ae/apply?transaction_id=FV-XXXXXXXX&token=SIGNED_TOKEN`
3. Clozer verifies the token (shared `CLOZER_REDIRECT_SECRET`) or calls verify endpoint.
4. Clozer fetches transaction data: `GET /api/clozer/transactions/FV-XXXXXXXX`
5. Customer completes Clozer application (prefilled from API response).
6. Clozer sends payment updates: `POST /api/clozer/installment-updates`
7. Updates appear in customer dashboard at `/profile/installment-payments`.

---

## API endpoints

| Method | URL | Auth |
|--------|-----|------|
| GET | `{API_BASE}/clozer/transactions/{transaction_id}` | Bearer or X-API-Key |
| POST | `{API_BASE}/clozer/installment-updates` | Bearer or X-API-Key + webhook signature |
| GET | `{API_BASE}/clozer/verify-redirect/{transaction_id}?token=...` | Bearer or X-API-Key |
| GET | `{API_BASE}/clozer/sample-transaction` | Bearer or X-API-Key (non-production only) |

---

## Transaction API response (example)

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "transaction_id": "FV-A1B2C3D4",
    "full_name": "Ahmed Mohammed",
    "emirates_id_number": "784-XXXX-XXXXXXX-X",
    "eid_expiry_date": "2028-05-30",
    "cif": "FV-SAMPLE01",
    "email": "customer@example.com",
    "mobile": "+971501234567",
    "total_invoice_amount": 5500,
    "monthly_installment_amount": 550,
    "number_of_installments": 10,
    "service_description": "Asset Purchase — Sample Property"
  }
}
```

**Note:** Transaction IDs use format `FV-XXXXXXXX` (8 hex chars). CIF uses `FV-{first8OfUserUuid}`.

---

## Webhook signature

HMAC-SHA256 of the **raw JSON body** using `CLOZER_WEBHOOK_SECRET`:

```
X-Clozer-Signature: sha256=<hex>
```

### Webhook payload (example)

```json
{
  "transaction_id": "FV-A1B2C3D4",
  "status": "approved",
  "installment_number": 1,
  "amount_paid": 550,
  "total_paid": 550,
  "total_amount": 5500
}
```

Recognized paid statuses: `approved`, `active`, `completed`, `paid`, `succeeded`.

---

## Test commands (development)

```bash
# Fetch sample transaction shape
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_CLOZER_API_KEY" \
  http://localhost:4000/api/clozer/sample-transaction

# Verify redirect token
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_CLOZER_API_KEY" \
  "http://localhost:4000/api/clozer/verify-redirect/FV-XXXXXXXX?token=TOKEN"

# Send test webhook (signature optional when NODE_ENV !== production)
curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/clozer/installment-updates \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_CLOZER_API_KEY" \
  -d "{\"transaction_id\":\"FV-XXXXXXXX\",\"status\":\"approved\",\"installment_number\":1,\"amount_paid\":550,\"total_paid\":550,\"total_amount\":5500}"
```

---

## User profile — Emirates ID (required for installments)

Users must complete Emirates ID in profile before Clozer checkout:

```json
{
  "emiratesId": {
    "fullName": "Ahmed Mohammed",
    "number": "784-XXXX-XXXXXXX-X",
    "expiryDate": "2028-05-30"
  }
}
```

Profile UI: Profile → Emirates ID section.

---

## Security notes

- All APIs must use HTTPS in production.
- Never expose `CLOZER_API_KEY`, `CLOZER_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, or `CLOZER_REDIRECT_SECRET` in frontend code.
- Redirect tokens expire after 15 minutes.
- All Clozer events are logged server-side as `[ClozerAudit]`.
